<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil softer as buyers stay away.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil softer as buyers stay away.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7563)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     33.30/33.70     18.96/19.19   33.50/33.90</p>
<p> BREMEN		33.30/33.70     18.96/19.19   33.50/33.90</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.50/33.90     19.07/19.30   33.60/34.00</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   34.20/34.60     19.47/19.70   34.30/34.70</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   34.20/34.60     19.47/19.70   34.30/34.70</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  36.00/36.40     20.50/20.73   36.10/36.50</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were unchanged to softer as a firmer dollar continued to dull demand. Traders said business was thin but firmer Rotterdam markets were supportive though competition for business was still strong.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7456</p>
